From d1258f8684e9093437bf7a0ba65a9b36fe4a73de Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: MasherDon <62326358+MasherDon@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 00:56:34 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 73/92] llama, deepseek4 : Engram's rows gathered by a CPU op
 of the graph right before the layer's first reader, not in set_input
 (SiegeLadder G23 step 2, on by default; LLAMA_ENGRAM_LATE=0 - off;
 decode-sized ubatches)

With the decode graph reused (G23 step 1) nothing stood between Engram's read-ahead (G26, page faults on a 189 GiB
mapping) and set_input any more - its wait was back on the card's path. Now set_input only writes the history and keeps
the ubatch; a ggml_custom_4d op per engram layer (made at the first reader: runahead's pass of the layer before, or the
layer itself) joins the read-ahead and gathers the rows, so the layers before the engram layer give the faults their
time back. The gather itself moved into fill_layer, which the classic path (prompt ubatches) calls as before.
Checks (SiegeLadder oracle o45): exact runahead and exact without runahead - text = trace (6 of 6 exact runs);
ABBA: the default mode 15.08 -> 15.42 tok/s (+2.2%), exact runahead 14.45 -> 14.69 (+1.7%).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
